cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SmashTable: Vectorized Associative Containers with Atomic Commits Spanning Several at Once"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/ashvardanian/SmashTable
url: https://github.com/ashvardanian/SmashTable
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22030408
abstract: >-
  SmashTable is a header-only C++ 20 library of associative containers, from vectors, AVL,
  weight-balanced and hash trees to immutable B-trees, S+ trees and Elias-Fano sets, whose
  transactional stores let one update span several containers so that every change lands or none
  does. A group stages into every container before the first one writes, each store declares its
  isolation level at compile time, ordered searches compare a whole row per vectorized pass, and
  the commit protocols are verified as Promela models and GenMC clients. It runs on CPUs, with a
  pinned atomic hash table that also runs on GPUs, and backs the in-memory engine of the UStore
  database.
keywords:
  - associative container
  - transactions
  - multiversion concurrency control
  - simd
  - b-tree
  - hash table
  - formal verification

authors:
